    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d743">

                <pb facs="0835" n="641" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC (PC)/8–945: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 743<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Alternate Delegate to the Preparatory
                        Commission of the United Nations</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerig</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Director of the Office of Special Political
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hiss</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d743-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-08-09T16:00:00+01:00">August 9, 1945—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>8019. For Hiss from Gerig.</p>
                <p>Your <hi rendition="#small-caps">Preco</hi> 23,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d743-f2"/>
                    Jebb informs he discussed question of officers ExCom (Executive Committee) and
                    PreCo (Preparatory Committee) on margin of Potsdam conference with Dunn Gromyko
                    and others and that rotation principle for ExCom was suggested for
                    consideration. Soviet group seemed favorable but have not yet replied
                    definitely;…</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d743-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d743-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the Secretary of State over the signature of Winant.</p>
